  "body": "file:///C:/foo/bar parses ok using the state machine, but file:///C|/foo/bar flags a syntax violation in the path state because | is not a URL code point while it's scanning for the / at end of the C| path segment:\r\n\r\n2. Otherwise, run these steps:\r\n    If c is not a URL code point and not \"%\", syntax violation.\r\n\r\nIs that intended? C| is not the normalised window drive letter form, but it's not clear from any of the narrative it's a syntax violation.",
